# Copy to config.env (next to this file) and pick one provider.
# config.env is loaded by every action; do not commit it.

# --- Local, free, nothing leaves your machine (recommended) -----------------
# Requires a running Ollama with the model pulled:
#   brew install ollama && ollama serve && ollama pull qwen2.5-coder
LUMEN_AI_PROVIDER=ollama
LUMEN_AI_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder

# --- Hosted providers ------------------------------------------------------
# Faster and usually better, but each action sends your diff to the provider
# and costs money per press. Uncomment one, comment out the Ollama block above.
#
# Valid LUMEN_AI_PROVIDER values: openai, groq, claude, ollama, opencode-zen,
# openrouter, deepseek, gemini, xai, vercel
#
# LUMEN_AI_PROVIDER=gemini
# LUMEN_AI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# LUMEN_API_KEY=...
#
# LUMEN_AI_PROVIDER=openai
# LUMEN_AI_MODEL=gpt-5-mini
# LUMEN_API_KEY=...

# lumen also reads the provider's own key variable (OPENAI_API_KEY,
# GEMINI_API_KEY, ...) and ~/.config/lumen/lumen.config.json, so if you already
# configured lumen with `lumen configure` you may not need this file at all.
